  "disclosures": [
    "T5 is a coverage arm (#127 rule P-coverage; funded by the measured projection): secondary, reported, never in the program claim.",
    "T5's configuration was selected on the policy split among three pre-declared configurations (native, ar4, native-2x); U had no such tuning (#127).",
    "64 x 64 frames (DIAMOND's native resolution; 4:3 -> 1:1 area resize): pigs are a few pixels wide; the readiness ceiling on true 64 x 64 frames measures what the readout can recover.",
    "The launch enters through the official action table in the csgo branch's real-valued form (launch5 @ act_emb[0].weight); the static context is the decision frame x4 (the pre-launch scene is static).",
    "Stochastic sampler; 8 paths per candidate with common random numbers; the readout is fitted on fit frames only (once, shared) and frozen before any evaluation read; z0 is the readout of the decision frame (the arm sees pixels only).",
    "No native success head (DIAMOND's reward / termination model predicts Atari rewards; not trained here): no native-head score and no U + head control; G-collapse not applied (pixel state through a readout; G-readout applies).",
    "P-novelty: after the primary scoring pass, T5 (if its guards pass) is scored on the #110 novelty levels from each level's decision frame (--score-novelty); descriptive only, no tokens."
  ],
